course: dictionary
lesson: 15081
title: Ripeness: ready and at its best
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ripeness is a noun. It names the state of something being fully grown and ready. Fruit that is ripe is ready to eat or pick. «Mia checked the ripeness of the pear by pressing it gently.» Mia is testing whether the pear is ready, so ripeness means how ready it is.
explain: You can check ripeness with your senses: colour, smell and softness. «The banana was yellow and sweet-smelling, so Sam knew it had reached its ripeness.» A green banana is not ripe yet. When you are not sure, look at the words around it: they tell you whether ripeness is about fruit or about something else.
explain: Ripeness can also mean being fully developed or ready for something to happen. In the phrase «the ripeness of time», it means the moment when everything is ready. The same word works for fruit and for ideas, so always ask what is ready in the sentence.
fact: Ripeness is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say «the ripeness», not «a ripeness».
fact: Ripening is a chemical change that happens inside fruit as it becomes ready to eat.
fact: Some fruits ripen faster near bananas, because bananas give off a gas called ethylene.
fact: «Ripe» means fully grown and ready to eat; «unripe» means not ready yet.
fact: The phrase «at the peak of ripeness» means at its very best point of being ready.
exercise: «Mia checked the ripeness of the pear by pressing it gently.» What does ripeness mean here? | The colour of the box the pear came in | *The state of being fully grown and ready to eat | The weight of the pear in the bag | The shape of the pear's stalk
exercise: How can you check the ripeness of a fruit? | Weigh it on the kitchen scales | *Look at its colour, smell it and feel how soft it is | Count its seeds only | Read the name on the shop label
exercise: «The plan was ready, and the ripeness of the idea was clear to everyone.» What does ripeness mean here? | *Being fully developed and ready | Being old and broken | Being hidden from view | Being very large and heavy
test:
«The farmer waited for the ripeness of the wheat before cutting it.» What does ripeness mean? | Being green and hard | *Being fully grown and ready to pick | Being very cold | Being broken into pieces
Which fruit can ripen faster when it is kept near bananas? | Carrots | *Avocados | Stones
exam:
When is fruit at the peak of ripeness? | Just before it is ready to eat | *When it is at its very best and fully ready to eat | When it has gone brown and rotten | When it is still hard and green
